  "body": "*Moved from https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-js-sdk/issues/341*\r\n\r\n/unban is broken on clients that use `/rooms/{roomId}/state/leave` to unban users instead of `/rooms/{roomId}/unban`.  The user will receive the following error:\r\n\r\n> Cannot leave user who was banned\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/f0e4bac64e8a4eff8132afcfc8406ce5fac11369/synapse/handlers/room_member.py#L228\r\n\r\nThe cause is [this line](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/f0e4bac64e8a4eff8132afcfc8406ce5fac11369/synapse/handlers/room_member.py#L225): when using the old/alternative method of unbanning users, `action` will be `\"leave\"` instead of `\"unban\"`.\r\n\r\nHowever, fixing this without also updating the client(s) will result in the return of https://github.com/vector-im/riot-web/issues/1961, which is likely fixed at the moment.  This is because the server will be unable to differentiate between /kick and /unban.  matrix-js-sdk will need to be updated to use [what I assume is the \"new\" API call](http://matrix.org/docs/spec/client_server/r0.2.0.html#post-matrix-client-r0-rooms-roomid-kick).",
